@startuml
!define RECTANGLE class

'RECTANGLE TengineLite {
'  - Inference engine for neural networks
'  - Cross-platform support
'  - Lightweight design
'}

RECTANGLE CoreModules {
  RECTANGLE DeviceModule {
    - NN Operators backend
  }
  
  RECTANGLE SchedulerModule {
    - Scheduling NNIR execution
    - Managing computation graphs
    - Hardware resource allocation
    - Model serializer coordination
  }
  
  RECTANGLE OperatorModule {
    - Registering NN Operators
    - Initializing NN Operators
  }
  
  RECTANGLE SerializerModule {
    - Decoding binary tmfile models
    - Producing serialized model parameters
  }
}

RECTANGLE APILayer {
  RECTANGLE CAPI {
    - Original Tengine-compatible interface
    - Primary integration path
  }
  
  RECTANGLE CppAPI {
    - C++ documentation entry points
  }
  
  RECTANGLE PythonAPI {
    - Python documentation entry points
  }
}

RECTANGLE ExampleApplications {
  - Classification (MobileNet v1)
  - Facial Landmark Detection
  - SSD Object Detection
  - RetinaFace Face Detection
  - Yolact Instance Segmentation
  - U-Net Image Segmentation
  - YoloV3/YoloV4-tiny/YoloV5s
  - NanoDet
  - EfficientDet
  - OpenPose
  - HRNet
  - CRNN Chinese Character Recognition
}

RECTANGLE ModelConversion {
  RECTANGLE LinuxConverter {
    - Pre-compiled tool
    - Linux-only execution
  }
  
  RECTANGLE BrowserConverter {
    - WebAssembly-based
    - Local execution in browser
    - No data upload guarantee
  }
}

CoreModules --> APILayer : Exposes functionality
APILayer --> ExampleApplications : Enables examples
SerializerModule --> ModelConversion : Supports conversion
ModelConversion --> ExampleApplications : Supplies models

note top of CoreModules : Four core architectural modules\nform the foundation

note right of APILayer : Three API surfaces provide\nintegration paths

note right of ModelConversion : Dual conversion approaches\nensure broad compatibility

note bottom of ExampleApplications : Comprehensive example set\ndemonstrates capabilities

title Tengine Lite System Architecture

@enduml